DirtyPipe (CVE-2022-0847) exploits a race condition in pipe buffer handling (`pipe->bufs`) where `splice()` and `sendpage()` fail to clear `PIPE_BUF_FLAG_CAN_MERGE`. An attacker overwrites root-owned `/etc/passwd` via:

```c
int fd = open("/etc/passwd", O_RDWR);
char buf[4096];
// Fill pipe with malicious payload
write(pipefd[1], buf, 4096);
splice(pipefd[0], NULL, fd, NULL, 4096, SPLICE_F_MOVE);
close(fd);
```

Defense-in-depth in Kubernetes:
- Linux kernel ≥ 5.17 with backported DirtyPipe fix (`CONFIG_PIPE`).
- Read-only root filesystem (`securityContext.readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`).
- SELinux `deny_ptrace` and `no_new_privs`.
- Falco rules detect `unlink`/`truncate` anomalies on `/etc/passwd`.

